                "event": "Winter Weather Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 11 at 11:02PM AKST until November 12 at 5:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Freezing rain and rain falling on cold surfaces expected.\nTotal ice accumulation of a light glaze.\n\n* WHERE...Lower Matanuska Valley and Southern Susitna Valley from\nsouth and west of Wasilla to Willow.\n\n* WHEN...Until 5 AM AKST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Some roads will become slick.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Areas of light rain, possibly mixed with snow,\nwill develop and become more widespread tonight. Temperatures will\nhover right around or a few degrees above freezing for locations\nsouth and west of Wasilla and below freezing near Willow. Colder\nareas, including hills, bridges, and overpasses will be the most\nlikely to see freezing rain. Rain will then taper off overnight\ninto Thursday morning, with temperatures cooling to freezing or\nbelow. Thus, any water on roadways will freeze.",
                "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. For the latest road\nconditions call 5 1 1 or visit 511.alaska.gov.",
                "response": "Execute",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
