                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 11 at 11:02PM AKST until November 12 at 5:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Freezing rain expected. Total ice accumulation of a light\nglaze.\n\n* WHERE...Anchorage and Eagle River.\n\n* WHEN...Until 5 AM AKST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Some roads will become slick.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Areas of light rain will develop by late this\nevening and continue into the overnight hours, mainly from Eagle\nRiver south to the Anchorage Bowl. Air temperatures will be right\naround freezing, leading to a light glaze of ice on area roads.\nRain will taper off by early Thursday morning, but roads will\nremain slick until temperatures warm later in the morning.",
